# UX workflow: edit a step note directly with rapid macro-encoder movements,
# let the coalesced history entry settle, then undo and redo it.
# Purpose: validates that direct step-property edits behave like one user
# action instead of one undoable entry per intermediate encoder value.
# Expect: capture_match:step_enabled=note_undone_closed, capture_match:note_committed=note_redone_closed

0 scenario sequencer
50 capture screen initial

# Move from Track to Pattern so macro turns edit the visible step property.
150 tap NAV 60

# Create an enabled step so the direct note edit is clearly visible.
300 tap MACRO_1 60
500 capture screen step_enabled

# One continuous direct edit gesture: several encoder values, one final note.
600 encoder MACRO_1 1.00
700 encoder MACRO_1 5.00
800 encoder MACRO_1 9.33
1000 capture screen note_pending
1400 capture screen note_committed

# Undo the coalesced note edit. The step remains enabled, but returns to C3.
1500 button LEFT_CENTER down
2500 tick
2550 capture screen undo_layer
2600 tap LEFT_TOP 60
4100 capture screen note_undone
4200 button LEFT_CENTER up
4400 capture screen note_undone_closed

# Redo the coalesced note edit.
4500 button LEFT_CENTER down
5500 tick
5550 capture screen redo_layer
5600 tap LEFT_BOTTOM 60
7100 capture screen note_redone
7200 button LEFT_CENTER up
7400 capture screen note_redone_closed
